#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""Physical Desktop Test Battery for Tamlinux 0.6.2 (tam-desktop-test).

Executes a watchable, automated sequence of Wayland input events
(pointer motions, clicks, drags, keychords, text typing, scroll wheel)
on the live Tamlinux graphical desktop (Hyprland + Quickshell) across 6 phases:
  Phase 0: Preflight & State Snapshot
  Phase 1: Top Bar, Start Menu & Shell Overlays
  Phase 2: Multi-Monitor Workspaces (0.5s pace) -> Staging Workspace 10
  Phase 3: Keybinding Explorer (Search, Card Verification & Capture Inhibitor)
  Phase 4: Foot, Micro, TUI Clipboard & Text Macros
  Phase 5: Tiling, Mouse-Follow (V12) & Safe Close Controls (K22, K25, K46)
  Phase 6: Restore Starting State & Postflight Audit

Emergency Stop:
  - Global reserved keybinding: Meta + Shift + Escape -> tam-desktop-test --stop
  - Physical mouse grab detection: moving the physical mouse aborts instantly
  - Ctrl+C (SIGINT) / SIGUSR1
"""

